{"seq":17,"trial_id":"shared-brain-access-2026-11/openclaw-opus-gbrain-open-mu-v031-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-22T09:46:54.613Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"d357e5d57082db0610bf72c74d59ccf08657e670bac56bf94465405cd2725e61","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","text":"Hi Dana, I went through all of Moss's notes in the shared files. Two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers come up:\n\n• *#PD-4492*, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell filed it on 4 Oct 2025: drivers at Eau Claire Dock Doors 14–18 weren't getting SMS bay assignments at gatehouse kiosk check-in. Support patched it that evening and Thea confirmed the fix on 5 Oct. There was a follow-up to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n• *#4419*, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 for scanner firmware testing.\n\nMoss's 9/14/2025 pipeline digest and 3/23/2026 renewal check-in also mention QFL, but neither has a ticket number. The cheat sheet notes that Quarendon Freightways (one \"r\") is a different company and not a customer, so nothing from that one is included. One more thing: the cheat sheet has no date, so I can't tell how current #4419 is."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
